      "fine_trace_step": 1,
      "description": "Source. While parsing the attacker-controlled `%.4294629629s` field, `mrb_str_format()` invokes `get_num()` on the decimal precision digits so they become vulnerability-relevant numeric state in `prec`."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "r_precision_value_must_fit_int",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "mrbgems/mruby-sprintf/src/sprintf.c",
      "function": "get_num",
      "line": 276,
      "operands": [
        "next_n",
        "INT_MAX"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "le",
        "left": "next_n",
        "right": "INT_MAX"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_precision_value_must_fit_int",
      "fine_trace_step": 3,
      "description": "Root cause fixed by the patch. `get_num()` narrows the parsed decimal value from `mrb_int next_n` into 32-bit `int` without first checking whether it fits in `INT_MAX`, so oversized numeric format specifiers become negative `prec`/`width` values instead of being rejected."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_negative_push_len_sink",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "mrbgems/mruby-sprintf/src/sprintf.c",
      "function": "mrb_str_format",
      "line": 841,
      "operands": [
        "len",
        "0"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "lt",
        "left": "len",
        "right": "0"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_negative_push_len_at_sink",
      "fine_trace_step": 8,
      "description": "AddressSanitizer crash site. `mrb_str_format()` passes the negative `len` derived from the malformed precision into `PUSH`, whose macro expansion reaches `memcpy(&buf[blen], s, l)` with `l < 0` and triggers the saved `negative-size-param` abort."
    },
